# What gets uploaded to Vercel on `vercel deploy`.
#
# Without this file the CLI falls back to .gitignore, which does not cover the
# same ground: a stale local `build/` output tree was uploaded on every deploy,
# pushing the payload past 400 MB and tripping the 100 MB per-file limit on a
# webpack cache blob. Vercel installs dependencies and runs the build itself, so
# it only ever needs sources, configuration and public assets.
#
# IMPORTANT: because this file exists, .gitignore is NO LONGER consulted for
# deployments. Anything sensitive or heavy must be listed here explicitly — most
# of all the env files below.
#
# Every directory rule is anchored with a leading slash so it can only ever
# match at the repository root. Unanchored, `/Products` would also match
# `src/app/(storefront)/products` and silently delete the catalog routes from
# the deployment.

# Secrets. Real values are configured as Vercel environment variables; a local
# .env.local must never be uploaded into a build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed and generated by Vercel during the build.
/node_modules
/.next
/out
/build
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local history and tooling.
/.git
/.github
/.cursor
/.vercel
/coverage

# Multi-gigabyte local asset libraries. The deployed app reads catalog imagery
# from Cloudflare R2 and catalog data from Neon, never from these folders.
/Products
/images
/bestListings
/data
/.cache

# Local-only review/scratch output, regenerated on demand.
/normalized-thumbnails
/.tmp-preview
